invariant: INV-22
file: srv_tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-nonblocking server sends its Certificate and CertificateVerify on a
  handshake a ticket authenticated. The resumed flight is
  EncryptedExtensions and Finished alone, and a client that resumes reads
  a Certificate there as a message out of turn, which is also what the
  QUIC Interop Runner's resumption case fails a server for.
  test/tcp_nonblocking_resume_tests.h resumes a ticket between this tree's two
  tcp-nonblocking drivers and counts the records the server sent.

--- old
    // A resumed handshake sends neither message: the ticket's PSK
    // authenticates this server.
    if (!sel->psk_selected) {
--- new
    if (1) {
